Use code with caution.2. Python Script ExampleUse the requests library to make RPC calls.
#python

import requests
import json

# RPC connection details
url = "http://127.0.0.1:18443"
user = "admin"
password = "admin123"

def bitcoin_rpc(method, params=[]):
    payload = {
        "jsonrpc": "1.0",
        "id": "curltext",
        "method": method,
        "params": params
    }
    response = requests.post(
        url,
        data=json.dumps(payload),
        auth=(user, password)
    )
    return response.json()

# --- Example Interactions ---

# 1. Get Blockchain Info
print("Blockchain Info:", bitcoin_rpc("getblockchaininfo"))

# 2. Generate new blocks (required to mine coins in regtest)
# Generates 101 blocks to make coinbase reward spendable
print("Mining blocks:", bitcoin_rpc("generatetoaddress", [101, "bcrt1q...your_address..."]))

# 3. Get Wallet Balance
print("Balance:", bitcoin_rpc("getbalance"))
Use code with caution.
3. Common Regtest Commands
Generate blocks: bitcoin-cli -regtest generatetoaddress 1 <address>
Get new address: bitcoin-cli -regtest getnewaddress
Check balance: bitcoin-cli -regtest getbalance
If you receive connection errors, confirm the rpcport matches the one specified in bitcoin.conf (18443 or 8332).
